Error [jet.UseAfterMove]: `t` was consumed by `.join()`, so it can't be used here
  --> tests/ui/task_double_join.jet:4:9
    |
  4 |     b: ^t.join() ?? 0
    |         ^
  --> tests/ui/task_double_join.jet:3:9
    |
  3 |     a: ^t.join() ?? 0
    |         ^ `t` moved to `.join()` here
 Why: After a value moves somewhere else, its old name no longer gives access to it
 Fix: Stop using `t` after the move, or give `.join()` a copy with `t.copy()` where it moved.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0121
